---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import pages from "../../data/pages.json";
---

<SiteLayout metadata={pages["/templates/"]}>
  <main id="main" class="growth-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <a href="/tools/">Resources</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <span aria-current="page">A useful starting point for your notes.</span>
      </nav>
      <header class="growth-hero">
        <div class="eyebrow">The documentation library</div>
        <h1>A useful starting point for your notes.</h1>
        <p>
          We’ve brought the structure, examples, and blank templates together so
          you can work through a format before adding it to your practice.
        </p>
      </header>
      <div class="resource-cards">
        <a class="resource-card" href="/templates/soap-notes/">
          <span class="tag">Four-part format</span>
          <h3>SOAP note template</h3>
          <p>
            Separate subjective and objective information, then document your
            assessment and plan.
          </p>
          <span class="text-link">Explore SOAP ↗</span>
        </a>
        <a class="resource-card" href="/templates/dap-notes/">
          <span class="tag">Three-part format</span>
          <h3>DAP note template</h3>
          <p>Organize the session into Data, Assessment, and Plan.</p>
          <span class="text-link">Explore DAP ↗</span>
        </a>
        <a class="resource-card" href="/blog/soap-vs-dap-notes/">
          <span class="tag">Format guide</span>
          <h3>SOAP vs. DAP</h3>
          <p>See how the same fictional session fits each structure.</p>
          <span class="text-link">Compare the formats ↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <section class="growth-split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Read, adapt, review</span>
          <h2>Keep the encounter at the center.</h2>
          <p>
            Use the prompts to organize what happened. Add the details required
            by your setting, payer, and professional standards. A template
            cannot determine what care was delivered or whether a record is
            complete.
          </p>
          <p>
            These are educational drafts from Otto editorial. Clinical review is
            pending.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="growth-note">
          <h3>From template to workflow</h3>
          <p>
            Otto describes AI-drafted SOAP and DAP notes with clinician review
            and signature. Watch the product walkthrough, then evaluate the
            process with a fictional session.
          </p>
          <a class="button" href="/demo/#watch">
            Watch the Otto demo ↗
          </a>
          <a class="text-link" href="/ai-progress-notes/">
            Explore AI progress notes ↗
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
    <section class="cta-section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="cta">
          <div>
            <h2>Make more room for the work you love.</h2>
            <p>
              See how Otto brings notes, scheduling, telehealth, and payments
              into your practice day.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a class="button light" href="/waitlist/">
            Join the waitlist <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
